1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Hi everyone, I'm Liv, I'm User Experience Designer on the Burp Scanner Development Team

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:10,880
and today I'm here to talk a little bit about the changes that we've made to the dashboard as well

3
00:00:10,880 --> 00:00:15,760
as some improvements and features that we've added to. So I'll jump into a project file.

4
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:20,480
The first and most important thing to note is that we've moved the event log and all issues

5
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:25,200
into a bottom drawer. For the event log this gives you more space to view the event details

6
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,880
but the bottom drawer is also global so it can be accessed from anywhere in Burp.

7
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:32,640
And this meant if you wanted to check any event log items or new issues

8
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:35,920
you can open it from wherever you are rather than having to go back to the dashboard.

9
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:42,240
For all new issues you can now delete single and multiple issues and additionally and this has

10
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:47,440
been in since November but we've added the ability to filter by b-check, scan and extension generated

11
00:00:47,440 --> 00:00:52,400
issues to make it easier to find what you're looking for. If any events happen or any issues

12
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:56,880
are found whilst the bottom drawer is closed you'll get notification dots based on the severity of the

13
00:00:56,880 --> 00:01:02,560
issue. Jumping into the main view of the dashboard now and we've moved tasks into a menu on the left

14
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:08,000
hand side of the screen. In the left hand panel you'll see any lie tasks, scans or intruder tasks.

15
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:13,040
From here you can see the status of your task and you can also reorder and rename your tasks as well.

16
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:16,160
You can also resize the side panel to make it suit your workspace.

17
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,680
Moving into the detail of the task cards this has largely stayed the same as when you could pop them out.

18
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:27,360
However we've added a task summary for anything with an audit you'll see on the summary view

19
00:01:27,360 --> 00:01:32,640
the most serious vulnerabilities ranked by severity and for crawl specific tasks we've displayed

20
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:37,520
what's been found and added to the sitemap. On the right hand side of any task you'll see a task

21
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:42,880
configuration in more detail and any progress when a task is running. And finally in the bottom right

22
00:01:42,880 --> 00:01:47,680
hand corner we've added a task log for when a task is running this will give a bit more detail as to what the

23
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:53,680
scanner is up to when it is running. We're really hoping the changes to the dashboard will improve

24
00:01:53,680 --> 00:02:07,680
your workflow so we'd love to hear if you have any thoughts or feedback. Thanks!

